  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 233 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nUpper level ridging continues to shift eastward through early next \nweek, engulfing much of the eastern CONUS by Tuesday. Although our \nregion will lie below the western edge of the ridge, decreasing \nheights coupled with southeasterly flow promotes a cooling trend. \nHighs in the 90s shall be prevalent Monday and Tuesday, though areas \nnear/along the river valleys and portions of the northeastern \nPermian Basin are progged to reach the low the low 100s. Wednesday \nonward, triple digit heat becomes restricted to areas along the Rio \nGrande valley. By late week, afternoon temperatures look to mainly \nrange in the low-to-mid 90s, with 80s in the higher terrain and much \nof southeast New Mexico. Along with the cooling trend, rain chances \nalso see an uptick as disturbances ride along the edge of the ridge. \nRain chances will tend to favor the western portions of our region \nmost afternoons, especially in the vicinity of the higher terrain. A \nfew long-range models show a cold front pushing in next weekend, \nbringing cooler temperatures and better rain chances. We will see \nhow this evolves as we head through the next several days.",
